===================================================================
STM32CubeIDE .gitignore
This file tells Git which files and folders to ignore in your project.
This is crucial for ensuring that only source code and essential
project configuration files are committed to the repository.
===================================================================
IDE workspace and user-specific files
These are specific to your local machine and should not be shared.

.metadata
.ide/
Build artifacts and output directories
These folders are generated when you compile your project. They can be
regenerated from source at any time, so they should not be in Git.

/Debug/
/Release/
/build/
Common build output files
These are the intermediate and final products of the compiler/linker.

*.o          # Object files
*.elf        # Executable and Linkable Format file
*.bin        # Binary firmware image
*.hex        # Intel HEX format firmware image
*.map        # Linker map file
*.lst        # Assembly listing file
*.su         # Stack usage file
*.d          # Dependency files (generated by the compiler)
*.swo        # Serial Wire Output trace files
Other generated files

*.bak        # Backup files
*.log        # Log files
*.tmp        # Temporary files
OS-generated files (macOS, Windows, Linux)

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
IMPORTANT:
The following files DEFINE your project and MUST be tracked by Git.
This .gitignore file is intentionally configured to NOT ignore them:
- .project (Identifies the folder as an IDE project)
- .cproject (Contains compiler/linker settings)
- .mxproject (Tracks CubeMX state within the IDE)
- *.ioc (The main STM32CubeMX configuration file)
- *.launch (Debug and run configurations)
- *.ld (Linker scripts, e.g., STM32..._FLASH.ld)